      "worked_solution": "In part 2, we found that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, computing the second derivative, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-3\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =2(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
