    "q-167318": {
      "dom_id": "question-167318",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "$\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x})\\,=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that $f(x)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\nWe apply the quotient rule, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}) & =\\frac{{f}^{′}(x)\\cdot (\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-f(x)\\cdot (\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{′}}{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{′}\\cdot (\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\cdot (\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{′}}{{sin}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x-(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}-3{sin}^{2}⁡x\\cancel{-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-3{cos}^{2}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)}{{sin}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
