    "q-167319": {
      "dom_id": "question-167319",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Given that $y=h(g(x)),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $){e}^{4{x}^{2}+8x+2}$",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that $y$ is a composite function:\n\n$$\ny={e}^{s},\\,s=2g=2(2{x}^{2}+4x+1)=4{x}^{2}+8x+2.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}s}={e}^{s},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}x}=8x+8.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}s}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{s}\\cdot (8x+8) \\\\  & =(8x+8)\\,{e}^{4{x}^{2}+8x+2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
