      "name": null,
      "problem": "$\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$+\\,C,\\,$ where $C$ is an arbitrary constant.",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C,\\,\\,\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+3\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
