    "q-167322": {
      "dom_id": "question-167322",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "$\\int (g(x)+\\sqrt{h(x)})\\,\\text{d}x\\,=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$+\\,C,\\,$ where $C$ is an arbitrary constant.",
      "worked_solution": "We combine the sum and the constant multiple rules, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (g(x)+\\sqrt{h(x)})\\text{d}x & =\\int (2{x}^{2}+4x+1+\\sqrt{{e}^{2x}})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (2{x}^{2}+4x+1+{e}^{x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+4\\int x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\,\\text{d}x+\\int {e}^{x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+4\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+x+{e}^{x}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}+2{x}^{2}+x+{e}^{x}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.",
